<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="Operation_and_Result">Operation and Result</span></h2>
<p>1. Place the white paper 1CM above the four bright white LED side of the sensor (hereinafter referred to as the front).<br />
2. Power on the development board. At this time, the LED port is connected to a high level, and the four high-bright white LEDs are on.<br />
3. Wait for more than 2 seconds after power on (white balance is being adjusted at this time).<br />
4. After the adjustment, please put the sensor facing the object to be measured, and the serial port outputs the corresponding RGB data.<br />
Refer to the color comparison table to know the detected color.<br />
</p>
<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="Precautions">Precautions</span></h2>
<p>1. Avoid the interference of external light during color recognition, otherwise it will affect the result of color recognition.<br />
Place the Color Sensor and light source etc. in a closed, non-reflective box for testing.<br />
2. White balance adjustment is required every time the Color Sensor module is restarted or the light source is replaced.<br />
</p>
